
========================================================================
P1  exact chi(G_delta) = #closed components (arcs + ISOLATED points); LRC <=> chi>0
========================================================================
  S=[1, 2, 3] delta=0.2 [strict]: chi(G)=4  LRC-holds(chi>0)? True
  S=[1, 2, 3] delta=0.25 [TIGHT (M=1/4)]: chi(G)=2  LRC-holds(chi>0)? True
  S=[1, 2, 3] delta=0.3 [covering]: chi(G)=0  LRC-holds(chi>0)? False
  S=[1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7] delta=0.1 [strict]: chi(G)=10  LRC-holds(chi>0)? True
  => at delta=1/4 the (1,2,3) good set is TWO isolated points {1/4,3/4}: chi=2>0 (weak loneliness),
     which the measure/volume misses. chi counts them; this is codex THM-2047's iff criterion.

========================================================================
P2  NERVE UPGRADE: chi(U)=nerve I-E sum(-1)^{|I|+1}[cap A_i!=0]  vs  measure I-E |U| (THM-1820 sinc)
========================================================================
  3 arcs at 0,1/3,2/3 halfwidth 0.1 [gaps (non-cover)]: nerve chi(U)=3 ; measure |U|=0.6000 ; cover(chi=0)? False
  3 arcs at 0,1/3,2/3 halfwidth 0.2 [overlap COVER]: nerve chi(U)=0 ; measure |U|=1.0000 ; cover(chi=0)? True
  (cover: chi(U)=3-3+0=0=chi(S^1); non-cover: chi(U)=3 gaps.) The nerve I-E computes covering EXACTLY.
  Contrast at the (1,2,3) tight threshold: MEASURE says covered, TOPOLOGY (chi) says lonely:
     delta=0.24: measure |U|=0.97333  chi(G)=2
     delta=0.25: measure |U|=1.00000  chi(G)=2
  => nerve/chi I-E (overlap indicators) upgrades THM-1820's measure I-E (lengths->sinc): the
     measure-zero tight witness that volume misses (S211) is exactly a nonzero nerve/chi term.

