P6  NEW equivariant sharpening: covering => iota:t->1-t FREE on G => chi EVEN => LRC <=> chi>=2 (mirror pair)
========================================================================
  S=[1, 2, 3] d=0.25 [tight, has even]: has_even=True, f_S(1/2)=0.000 (1/2 in G? False); chi(G)=2 [EVEN]
  S=[1, 2, 3] d=0.2 [strict, has even]: has_even=True, f_S(1/2)=0.000 (1/2 in G? False); chi(G)=4 [EVEN]
  S=[1, 3, 5, 7] d=0.3 [ALL ODD]: has_even=False, f_S(1/2)=0.500 (1/2 in G? True); chi(G)=1 [ODD]
  S={1..12,182} d=0.07143 [deep well (13-speed)]: has_even=True, f_S(1/2)=0.000 (1/2 in G? False); chi(G)=24 [EVEN]
  check mirror-pairing of components on the (1,2,3) tight case (should be {1/4,3/4}=iota pair):
     components at t ~ [0.25, 0.75]; closed under t->1-t (mirror pairs)? True
  => COVERING sets (which contain an even speed) have chi(G_delta) EVEN, so codex's chi>0 sharpens to
     chi>=2: LRC(14) <=> at least ONE mirror pair {t*,1-t*} of lonely windows survives. By iota-symmetry
     it suffices to find ONE lonely window in [0,1/2] -- an equivariant HALVING of Wall A. The kps-S19
     free-iota Gauss sum i*sqrt(7) is the ODD-equivariant obstruction living on this same involution.
